{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Persistence is Key"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "If At First You Don't Succeed"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Identify and describe issues relating to money, in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le10ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " What Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You shift emphasis from the beginning to another part of the sentence by using what, that and who phrases as subjects."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Usually, we focus on the person doing the action in this case.<br/> <span class=\"italic\">  Example: You want to impress them and look more confident. </span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "If we wish to place emphasis on another part of the sentence, we isolate that part and package up the rest of the information into a what-phrase (or sometimes a that clause.)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Example: What you want is to impress them and look more confident. </span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">What</span> </span>  or <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Who</span> </span>  serves as a placeholder for the content of the noun phrase that has been moved to the end of the sentence. The effect is that more emphasis is placed on the initial content.<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Example: What you can do to avoid this is to breath slowly through your nose.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The first part of the sentence is called a phrase because if you remove <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">what</span></span>, it causes the structure not to make sense: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><strike>What </strike>you could do is send a thank-you e-mail after the interview.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><strike>What</strike> I find particularly useful is to take a deep breath, listen to your body and wear a smile</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is how we form \u201cWhat\u201d clauses. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> subject / What-phrase</div> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">complement</div> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What I'm suggesting<br/> What I usually do<br/> What I've learned from my research</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">is <br/> is <br/> is</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">to find a sitting position that suits you.<br/> sit straight and maybe lean forward a bit.<br/> one should thank everyone promptly. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Asking for Extension"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Communication is a two-way street. It involves a lot of back and forth. Therefore, it is important to communicate when something is not clear to you or when you need more from the other speaker. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " Asking for extension is important in many situations especially when when the message being communicated is difficult or new in some way. Here are some ways you can ask for extension.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Could you expand on that?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Could you elaborate on that?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Uh, could you shed some light on this?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Could you be more specific?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Could you clarify that?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "land a job"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to get a job"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These tips will help you land a job."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents":